hi there steve again it's the last day  of the year  i'm still in england visiting with my  son and his family  uh  as often happens i think about language  learning i'm  certainly spending a fair amount of each  day um an hour or two anyway  with my farsi  occasionally looking back at my arabic  which i'm going to get back to when i  get back to vancouver  and today i want to talk about patience  patience and language learning because  actually the reason is because my  daughter-in-law said to me she said  steve you're not a very patient person  how can you  be so interested in language learning  and it's true i'm not patient i can't do  you know things with my hands like i had  a friend who bought balsa wood and cut  it up into small pieces and built boats  and then  slid them into bottles and then  carefully pulled the sails up so they  had a sailboat inside a bottle i mean i  couldn't possibly do that i think my  stomach would be all tied up in a knot i  can't sit there and do things patiently  like that  and so i kind of have come to the  conclusion that using the word patience  for  language learning is a bit misleading  it's more a matter of perseverance and  energy when i  you know day after day after day  listen and read and occasionally use the  language that i'm learning i'm just  going at it with perseverance and energy  i know that eventually it's going to get  me to my goal  it's like jogging or cross-country  skiing is it's it's an activity that  requires  you know endurance  and determination to stay with it  it's not so matter so much a matter of  patience  and you have to let things go like i it  doesn't bother me  that i forget things it doesn't bother  me that i  can't say things that i don't understand  things that i get the rules wrong or  make mistakes none of that bothers me i  just keep going it's like i'm  cross-country skiing or jogging i'm  going at it with energy every day i go  at it  i go at it because i know that  eventually i will reach my goal and  maybe that's why  you know i don't have the patience to  practice golf for example forever on the  range because i don't think i will  really improve but i know from  experience that as long as i keep  putting in the time  and i apply myself with energy to  language learning i will eventually  reach my goal  and  i think  it's important also  maybe this is a type of patience not the  patients where you sit there and do  things that are very tedious and  painstaking  but the patience to say that you know  when you start with a language you know  in that first  few weeks  you achieved tremendous uh uh success in  a way  you're all of a sudden able to say  things  you can say hello how are you  all kinds of things in a new language  it's a feeling of great success and then  you discover that to actually reach a  level where you understand what people  are saying  you know where because people are not  going to direct their conversation at  you in the few words that you know  people are going to talk about a variety  of things  to reach a level where you can  understand people understand movies and  read comfortably takes a long long time  so really  what is required  in a way perhaps it's a form of patience  but not the kind of patients that i  don't have  it's more a matter of staying with it  perseverance  energy  belief that you can get there  and of course considering it worthwhile  you have to consider it worthwhile or  you're not going to put that energy and  that perseverance into the task so it's  not the sort of painstaking patience  that's required it's continuing  commitment and a belief that you're  going to get there and so maybe that'll  be my new year's resolution but i don't  need to make that new year's resolution  because i have that level of commitment  but any of you who  at some level want to become fluent in  another language and  you know  occasionally sort of stop doing it or  lose confidence or get frustrated maybe  your new year's resolution should be to  commit yourself with energy to staying  with the task regardless  don't rely on patience rely on energy  and perseverance okay then and happy new  year to everyone bye for now  it suddenly dawned on me that i should  perhaps end up  the video in a few different languages  so uh  bono rosanne uh  i don't know that's good enough for now  bye for now  [Music]
 

